  <summary date="2026-10-20T14:36:45Z" status="Introduced in Senate">Military Spouse Hiring Act 

This bill allows&#160;employers to claim a tax credit for a percentage of qualified wages paid to an employee who is a military spouse by&#160;expanding the federal Work Opportunity Tax Credit (WOTC) to add qualified military spouses as a targeted group. (The WOTC applies to employers who hire members of specific targeted groups, such as veterans, ex-felons, and long-term unemployment recipients, and is generally equal to a percentage of the wages paid to such individuals&#160;in the first year of employment, up to a maximum amount. Under current law, the wages must be paid before 2026.)

The bill defines a qualified military spouse as any individual who is certified by a state workforce agency as being (as of the hiring date) a spouse of a member of the Armed Forces.</summary>
</bill>
